From: RockBase SDK <dev@rockbase.local>
Subject: [PATCH] dts: canaan: st7701-480x800: align DSI timing with RTOS (27MHz)

RockBase 480x800 ST7701 panel: lower the DSI pixel clock from 39.6MHz to
27MHz (and match RTOS mipi_st7701_480x800 porches: htotal 556, vtotal 868).

Why: with the old timing the DSI link runs at pclk*24/(2lanes*2) =
1.56Gbps per lane (canaan_dsi.c: clk*3*8/lanes/2). The RTOS firmware
drives the same panel at 27MHz = 569Mbps/lane. On the same unshielded
FPC flex cable, touching the MIPI ribbon under the 1.56Gbps link
reliably blacks out the display (EMI/ground-loop coupling), while the
569Mbps RTOS link is immune. Aligning the Linux timing to the RTOS
values restores the same link margin.

Refresh: 39.6MHz/1110 lines = 35.9Hz -> 27MHz/868 lines = 34.4Hz
(same as RTOS; fine for this status display).

Affects boards including display-st7701-480x800.dtsi (currently
k230-rockbase-lcd.dts, the RockBase board).

---
diff --git a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/display-st7701-480x800.dtsi b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/display-st7701-480x800.dtsi
index 1e76aa6..3fd339f 100644
--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/display-st7701-480x800.dtsi
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/canaan/display-st7701-480x800.dtsi
@@ -70,15 +70,18 @@
 
 		display-timings {
 			timing-0 {
-				clock-frequency = <39600000>;
+				/* RockBase: align with RTOS mipi_st7701 27MHz timing to
+				 * lower DSI lane rate (1.56G->569Mbps/lane) for EMI margin.
+				 * htotal=556, vtotal=868 -> 34.4Hz, matching RTOS. */
+				clock-frequency = <27000000>;
 				hactive = <480>;
 				vactive = <800>;
-				hfront-porch = <80>;
-				hback-porch = <20>;
-				hsync-len = <20>;
-				vfront-porch = <220>;
-				vback-porch = <70>;
-				vsync-len = <10>;
+				hfront-porch = <30>;
+				hback-porch = <10>;
+				hsync-len = <4>;
+				vfront-porch = <40>;
+				vback-porch = <20>;
+				vsync-len = <8>;
 			};
 		};
 
